@* ReviewPage: the view of one review at "/projects/{id}/reviews/{reviewId}", with its comment threads. The same page
   opens at "/projects/{id}/reviews/{reviewId}/files/{path}" (optionally with ?line=N&side=head|baseline) and at
   "/projects/{id}/reviews/{reviewId}/threads/{threadId}": stable links that open that file, scroll to and highlight
   that line or thread, and that the page keeps in the browser's address bar as the reader chooses files and threads.
   A link that names something that does not exist shows a message above the file list instead of an error page.

   Presentation only; state and event handling live in ReviewPage.razor.cs. From the top it shows the title, a
   one-sentence next step (checklist, threads and signatures) under an Approved / In review badge, the checklist
   progress with a link to the checklist page, the Reviewers card (slots with primary, alternate and signature
   status; an occupant of a slot signs there after confirming the password (an account of an identity provider
   confirms its identity at the provider with a button instead), or sees what blocks signing; an
   unsigned slot can be changed or removed and slots can be added), the
   list of files with size and open-thread count, the thread index of all files
   (filter All/Open/Resolved, default Open; choosing a row selects the file and highlights the lines), and for
   the selected file: for a file of a repository review with a baseline the diff (see DiffView) with a Diff / Head /
   Baseline selector (Head not for a deleted file, Baseline not for an added file), otherwise the text as numbered lines (or a notice for binary files), a form that starts a thread (under the
   selected line in the diff), and the threads of that file (a resolved thread is a one-line header until expanded;
   in the diff the threads are under their lines). The review id, state,
   content fingerprint, record digest and per-file SHA-256 hashes are last, in a Details section that is collapsed. All file
   and comment text is rendered as plain text. Every interactive element and every key value carries a stable
   kebab-case data-testid (file rows carry the list index, line and thread elements the line number or thread
   id), and the data-interactive marker on the root flips to "true" once the live circuit is connected.

   The page body is inside SessionGate, which replaces it with a "Session ended" message when the user is no longer
   valid while the page is open.

   An approved review is locked: a Locked badge and a banner explain it, and every control that would change the
   review (new thread, reply, resolve, line comments, reviewer slots) is disabled. A project or system administrator
   sees a reopen form (a reason of up to 250 characters is required); the reopen history is listed. When the project
   requires independent reviewers the author of the review is not offered as a reviewer and is told so.

   An optional due date (a UTC calendar day) is shown under the title with an Overdue badge when it lies before today
   (UTC) and the review is not approved. A project administrator or the creator of the review can set, change or
   clear it while the review is not locked; the service checks the same rule again. *@
@page "/projects/{ProjectId:int}/reviews/{ReviewId}"
@page "/projects/{ProjectId:int}/reviews/{ReviewId}/files/{**FilePath}"
@page "/projects/{ProjectId:int}/reviews/{ReviewId}/threads/{ThreadId:int}"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>@(Review?.Id ?? "Review") - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<SessionGate>
<main class="page review-page" data-testid="review-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/projects" data-testid="breadcrumb-projects-link">Projects</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a href="/projects/@ProjectId" data-testid="project-link">@(ProjectName ?? $"Project {ProjectId}")</a>
        @if (Review is not null)
        {
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span aria-current="page">@Review.Id</span>
        }
    </nav>

    @if (!Loaded)
    {
        <p class="muted" data-testid="review-loading">Loading...</p>
    }
    else if (Review is null)
    {
        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="review-not-found">Review '@ReviewId' does not exist in project @ProjectId.</p>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="title-row">
            <h1 data-testid="review-title">@Review.Title</h1>
            @if (Approval is not null)
            {
                <span class="badge @(Approval.IsApproved ? "approved" : null)" data-testid="review-approval">@(Approval.IsApproved ? "Approved" : "In review")</span>
                @if (IsLocked)
                {
                    <span class="badge locked" data-testid="review-locked">Locked</span>
                }
            }
            <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/reviews/@ReviewId/history" data-testid="history-link">History</a>
        </div>

        @* The due date is a UTC calendar day. Overdue means "before today (UTC) and not approved"; an approved review
           keeps its date as history. Only a project administrator or the creator sees the edit form, and only while
           the review is not locked *@
        <section class="due-date" data-testid="review-due-section">
            @if (Review.DueDate is { } dueDate)
            {
                <p class="status">
                    <span data-testid="review-due-date">Due @FormatDueDate(dueDate) (UTC)</span>
                    @if (IsOverdue)
                    {
                        <span class="badge failed" data-testid="review-overdue">Overdue</span>
                    }
                </p>
            }
            else
            {
                <p class="status muted" data-testid="review-due-none">No due date</p>
            }
            @* The refusal is shown even when the form is gone: the review may have been approved meanwhile *@
            @if (DueDateError is not null)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="review-due-error">@DueDateError</p>
            }
            @if (CanEditDueDate)
            {
                <form data-testid="due-date-form" novalidate @onsubmit="SaveDueDateAsync">
                    <div class="field">
                        <label for="review-due-input">Due date (a calendar day in UTC)</label>
                        <input id="review-due-input" type="date" data-testid="review-due-input" value="@DueDateInput"
                               @oninput="e => DueDateInput = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty" />
                    </div>
                    <button type="submit" data-testid="review-due-save">Save</button>
                    <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="review-due-clear" @onclick="ClearDueDateAsync">Clear</button>
                </form>
            }
        </section>

        @* A follow-up says which review it follows and how much it took over; a review that was followed up lists its
           follow-ups. Both are plain links: what was carried is marked on the checklist and on the threads themselves *@
        @if (Review.FollowsReviewId is { } follows)
        {
            <p class="status" data-testid="review-follows">
                Follows <a href="@ReviewLinks.ForReview(ProjectId, follows)" data-testid="review-follows-link">@follows</a>:
                <span data-testid="review-carried-counts">@Review.CarriedAnswerCount @(Review.CarriedAnswerCount == 1 ? "answer" : "answers") and @Review.CarriedThreadCount @(Review.CarriedThreadCount == 1 ? "thread" : "threads") carried</span>
            </p>
        }
        @if (FollowUps.Count > 0)
        {
            <p class="status" data-testid="review-followed-by">
                Followed by
                @for (var index = 0; index < FollowUps.Count; index++)
                {
                    var followUp = FollowUps[index];
                    @(index > 0 ? ", " : null)
                    <a href="@ReviewLinks.ForReview(ProjectId, followUp)" data-testid="review-followed-by-link-@followUp">@followUp</a>
                }
            </p>
        }

        @if (IsLocked)
        {
            <section class="card" data-testid="review-locked-banner">
                <p class="notice" role="status">
                    This review is approved and locked. Its content, checklist and reviewers can no longer change.
                    A project administrator can reopen it; the signatures are then kept as history and the review
                    must be signed again.
                </p>
                @if (CanReopen)
                {
                    <form data-testid="reopen-form" novalidate @onsubmit="ReopenAsync">
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="reopen-reason">Reason for reopening <span class="required">* required</span></label>
                            <textarea id="reopen-reason" rows="2" maxlength="@ReviewLimits.MaxReopenReasonLength"
                                      data-testid="reopen-reason" value="@ReopenReason"
                                      @oninput="e => ReopenReason = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty"></textarea>
                        </div>
                        @if (ReopenError is not null)
                        {
                            <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="reopen-error">@ReopenError</p>
                        }
                        <button type="submit" data-testid="reopen-button">Reopen review</button>
                    </form>
                }
            </section>
        }

        @if (Approval?.Reopens is { Count: > 0 } reopens)
        {
            <section class="card" data-testid="reopen-history">
                <h2>Reopen history</h2>
                <ul class="item-list">
                    @for (var n = 0; n < reopens.Count; n++)
                    {
                        var reopen = reopens[n];
                        <li data-testid="reopen-entry-@n">
                            <strong data-testid="reopen-by-@n">@reopen.ReopenedByDisplayName</strong>
                            <time class="muted" datetime="@reopen.ReopenedAt.UtcDateTime.ToString("O")" data-testid="reopen-time-@n">@FormatTime(reopen.ReopenedAt)</time>
                            <p data-testid="reopen-reason-@n">@reopen.Reason</p>
                            <p class="muted hint">Earlier record <span class="hash" data-testid="reopen-digest-@n">@ShortDigest(reopen.PreviousDigest)</span></p>
                        </li>
                    }
                </ul>
            </section>
        }

        @if (Approval?.IsApproved == true)
        {
            @* The signed PDF is offered only for a complete review, and only when the signing key can be used *@
            var attestationKey = AttestationKeys.Describe();
            <p class="status" data-testid="attestation">
                @if (attestationKey.IsAvailable)
                {
                    <a class="action outline" href="@ReviewLinks.ForAttestation(ProjectId, ReviewId)" download="@DemaConsulting.ReviewCenter.Evidence.AttestationService.FileNameFor(ProjectId, ReviewId)" data-testid="attestation-download-button">Download attestation (PDF)</a>
                    <span class="muted" data-testid="attestation-note">@AttestationNote(attestationKey.Info!)</span>
                    <a class="action outline small" href="/help/signed-attestation" data-testid="attestation-help-link">About attestations</a>
                    @foreach (var warning in attestationKey.Warnings)
                    {
                        <span class="notice warning" role="status" data-testid="attestation-key-warning">@warning</span>
                    }
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="error" role="alert" data-testid="attestation-key-problem">Attestation is unavailable: @attestationKey.Problem</span>
                }
            </p>
        }

        <p class="status"><strong>Next step:</strong> <span data-testid="next-step">@Approval?.NextStep</span></p>

        @if (UnreadCount > 0)
        {
            <p class="status" data-testid="review-unread-summary"><span class="badge unread">New</span> @UnreadSummary</p>
        }
        <section class="summary-strip" data-testid="review-summary" aria-label="Review summary">
            @if (Checklist is not null)
            {
                <div class="summary-cell" data-testid="checklist-card">
                    <span class="summary-label">Checklist</span>
                    <span class="summary-value" data-testid="checklist-progress-summary">@ChecklistSummary()</span>
                    <progress class="summary-progress" max="@Checklist.Overall.Total" value="@Checklist.Overall.Answered"
                              aria-label="Checklist progress"></progress>
                    <a class="action outline small" href="/projects/@ProjectId/reviews/@ReviewId/checklist" data-testid="checklist-link">Open checklist</a>
                </div>
            }
            @if (Approval is not null)
            {
                <div class="summary-cell" data-testid="summary-reviewers">
                    <span class="summary-label">Reviewers</span>
                    <span class="summary-value">@(Approval.Slots.Count == 0 ? "No reviewer slots yet" : $"{Approval.Slots.Count(s => s.State == SlotSignatureState.Signed)} of {Approval.Slots.Count} signed")</span>
                </div>
            }
            <div class="summary-cell" data-testid="summary-threads">
                <span class="summary-label">Threads</span>
                <span class="summary-value">@Threads.Count(t => t.State == ReviewThreadState.Open) open &middot; @Threads.Count(t => t.State == ReviewThreadState.Resolved) resolved</span>
            </div>
        </section>

        // The reviewers card is declared here and drawn after the files and threads, because reading comes first
        var approval = Approval;
        RenderFragment? reviewersCard = null;
        if (approval is not null)
        {
            reviewersCard = @<section class="card" data-testid="reviewers-card">
                <h2>Reviewers and signing</h2>
                @if (ShowAuthorHint)
                {
                    <p class="notice" data-testid="author-independence-hint">
                        You created this review, so a different project member has to review and sign it.
                    </p>
                }
                @if (approval.Slots.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="muted" data-testid="slots-empty">No reviewer slots yet.</p>
                }
                @foreach (var slot in approval.Slots)
                {
                    var slotId = slot.SlotId;
                    var occupant = IsOccupant(slot);
                    <div class="slot" data-testid="slot-@slotId">
                        <h3 data-testid="slot-label-@slotId">Slot @slot.Number</h3>
                        <p class="muted">Primary: <span data-testid="slot-primary-@slotId">@slot.Primary.DisplayName</span>
                            @if (!slot.Primary.IsMember)
                            {
                                <span class="badge"
                                      data-testid="slot-primary-not-member-@slotId">No longer a project member</span>
                            }
                            &middot; Alternate:
                            <span data-testid="slot-alternate-@slotId">@(slot.Alternate?.DisplayName ?? "None")</span>
                            @if (slot.Alternate is { IsMember: false })
                            {
                                <span class="badge"
                                      data-testid="slot-alternate-not-member-@slotId">No longer a project member</span>
                            }</p>
                        @if (!slot.Primary.IsMember || slot.Alternate is { IsMember: false })
                        {
                            <p class="muted hint" data-testid="slot-not-member-hint-@slotId">
                                A reviewer who is no longer a project member cannot sign until added to the project
                                again.
                            </p>
                        }
                        <p><span class="badge @SlotBadgeClass(slot)" data-testid="slot-status-@slotId">@SlotStatusLabel(slot)</span></p>

                        @if (slot.State == SlotSignatureState.NotSigned)
                        {
                            <details class="slot-edit">
                                <summary>Change reviewers</summary>
                                <select aria-label="Primary reviewer of slot @slot.Number" data-testid="slot-primary-select-@slotId"
                                        value="@PrimaryChoice(slot)" @onchange="e => SlotPrimaryChoices[slotId] = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty">
                                    @foreach (var candidate in VisibleCandidates)
                                    {
                                        <option value="@candidate.UserId">@candidate.DisplayName (@candidate.Username)</option>
                                    }
                                    @if (!IsOffered(slot.Primary))
                                    {
                                        <option value="@slot.Primary.UserId" data-testid="slot-primary-unavailable-@slotId">@UnavailableLabel(slot.Primary)</option>
                                    }
                                </select>
                                <select aria-label="Alternate reviewer of slot @slot.Number" data-testid="slot-alternate-select-@slotId"
                                        value="@AlternateChoice(slot)" @onchange="e => SlotAlternateChoices[slotId] = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty">
                                    <option value="">No alternate</option>
                                    @foreach (var candidate in VisibleCandidates)
                                    {
                                        <option value="@candidate.UserId">@candidate.DisplayName (@candidate.Username)</option>
                                    }
                                    @if (slot.Alternate is { } alternate && !IsOffered(alternate))
                                    {
                                        <option value="@alternate.UserId" data-testid="slot-alternate-unavailable-@slotId">@UnavailableLabel(alternate)</option>
                                    }
                                </select>
                                <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="slot-save-@slotId"
                                        aria-label="Save slot @slot.Number" @onclick="() => SaveSlotAsync(slot)">Save</button>
                                <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="slot-remove-@slotId"
                                        aria-label="Remove slot @slot.Number" @onclick="() => RemoveSlotAsync(slotId)">Remove</button>
                            </details>
                        }

                        @if (SlotErrors.TryGetValue(slotId, out var slotError))
                        {
                            <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="slot-error-@slotId">@slotError</p>
                        }

                        @if (occupant && slot.State != SlotSignatureState.Signed)
                        {
                            @if (approval.Blockers.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <div data-testid="sign-blockers-@slotId">
                                    <p>This review cannot be signed yet:</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        @foreach (var blocker in approval.Blockers)
                                        {
                                            <li>@blocker</li>
                                        }
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            }
                            else if (ReopenerBlocked)
                            {
                                <p class="notice" role="status" data-testid="reopener-cannot-sign-@slotId">
                                    You reopened this review; another reviewer must sign.
                                </p>
                            }
                            else if (CurrentIsExternal && !ConfirmedSlots.Contains(slotId))
                            {
                                <form method="post" action="/auth/oidc/reauth" data-testid="sign-reauth-form-@slotId">
                                    <AntiforgeryToken />
                                    <input type="hidden" name="projectId" value="@ProjectId" />
                                    <input type="hidden" name="reviewId" value="@ReviewId" />
                                    <input type="hidden" name="slotId" value="@slotId" />
                                    <input type="hidden" name="returnUrl" value="@ReviewAddress" />
                                    <p class="muted" data-testid="sign-meaning-@slotId">@SigningService.MeaningText</p>
                                    @if (!Oidc.Value.Enabled)
                                    {
                                        <p class="muted" role="status" data-testid="sign-reauth-off-@slotId">
                                            Signing in with an identity provider is switched off, so this review
                                            cannot be signed now. Ask an administrator.
                                        </p>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <p class="muted" data-testid="sign-reauth-hint-@slotId">
                                            To sign, confirm it is you: @Oidc.Value.DisplayName asks you to sign in
                                            again, then you come back here to sign.
                                        </p>
                                        @if (SignMessage(slotId) is { } reauthMessage)
                                        {
                                            <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="sign-error-@slotId">@reauthMessage</p>
                                        }
                                        <button type="submit" data-testid="sign-reauth-@slotId">
                                            Confirm identity with @Oidc.Value.DisplayName
                                        </button>
                                    }
                                </form>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <form data-testid="sign-form-@slotId" novalidate @onsubmit="() => SignAsync(slotId)">
                                    <p class="muted" data-testid="sign-meaning-@slotId">@SigningService.MeaningText</p>
                                    @if (CurrentIsExternal)
                                    {
                                        <p class="notice" role="status" data-testid="sign-confirmed-@slotId">
                                            Identity confirmed. Review the record, then sign.
                                        </p>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <div class="field">
                                            <label for="sign-password-@slotId">Confirm your password to sign</label>
                                            <input id="sign-password-@slotId" type="password" autocomplete="current-password"
                                                   data-testid="sign-password-@slotId" @key="@($"{slotId}-{PasswordKey}")"
                                                   @oninput="e => SignPasswords[slotId] = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty" />
                                        </div>
                                        @if (CurrentHasTotp)
                                        {
                                            <div class="field">
                                                <label for="sign-totp-@slotId">Current code from your authenticator app</label>
                                                <input id="sign-totp-@slotId" type="text" inputmode="numeric" maxlength="6"
                                                       autocomplete="one-time-code"
                                                       data-testid="sign-totp-@slotId" @key="@($"{slotId}-totp-{PasswordKey}")"
                                                       @oninput="e => SignTotpCodes[slotId] = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty" />
                                                <p class="muted hint">If you just signed in with this code, wait for the next one.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        }
                                    }
                                    @if (SignMessage(slotId) is { } signError)
                                    {
                                        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="sign-error-@slotId">@signError</p>
                                    }
                                    <button type="submit" data-testid="sign-button-@slotId">Sign</button>
                                </form>
                            }
                        }
                    </div>
                }

                <form class="slot-add" data-testid="slot-add-form" novalidate @onsubmit="AddSlotAsync">
                    <details open="@(approval.Slots.Count == 0 || NewSlotError is not null)">
                    <summary>Add a slot</summary>
                    @if (IsLocked)
                    {
                        <p class="muted hint" data-testid="slots-locked-hint">The reviewers cannot change while the review is locked.</p>
                    }
                    <select aria-label="Primary reviewer of the new slot" data-testid="new-slot-primary-select"
                            disabled="@IsLocked" data-locked="@LockedMarker"
                            value="@NewSlotPrimary" @onchange="e => NewSlotPrimary = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty">
                        <option value="">Choose a primary reviewer</option>
                        @foreach (var candidate in VisibleCandidates)
                        {
                            <option value="@candidate.UserId">@candidate.DisplayName (@candidate.Username)</option>
                        }
                    </select>
                    <select aria-label="Alternate reviewer of the new slot" data-testid="new-slot-alternate-select"
                            disabled="@IsLocked" data-locked="@LockedMarker"
                            value="@NewSlotAlternate" @onchange="e => NewSlotAlternate = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty">
                        <option value="">No alternate</option>
                        @foreach (var candidate in VisibleCandidates)
                        {
                            <option value="@candidate.UserId">@candidate.DisplayName (@candidate.Username)</option>
                        }
                    </select>
                    @if (NewSlotError is not null)
                    {
                        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="new-slot-error">@NewSlotError</p>
                    }
                    <button type="submit" disabled="@IsLocked" data-locked="@LockedMarker" class="@(approval.Slots.Count == 0 ? null : "secondary")" data-testid="new-slot-add-button">Add slot</button>
                    </details>
                </form>
            </section>;
        }

        <section class="card">
            <h2>Files</h2>
            @if (DeepLinkMessage is not null)
            {
                <p class="notice" role="alert" data-testid="deep-link-message">@DeepLinkMessage
                    <a class="action outline" href="@ReviewLinks.ForReview(ProjectId, ReviewId)" data-testid="deep-link-back">Back to the file list of this review</a></p>
            }
            <ul class="item-list" data-testid="files-list">
                @for (var index = 0; index < Review.Files.Count; index++)
                {
                    var file = Review.Files[index];
                    var fileIndex = index;
                    <li class="file-row @(file.Path == SelectedPath ? "selected" : null)" data-testid="file-row-@index">
                        <div class="path" data-testid="file-path-@index">@file.Path</div>
                        <div class="muted file-size">
                            @if (Review.IsFromRepository)
                            {
                                <span class="badge" data-testid="file-kind-@index">@file.ChangeKind</span>
                            }
                            <span data-testid="file-size-@index">@DisplaySize(file)</span> bytes &middot; <span data-testid="file-open-threads-@index">@OpenThreadLabel(file.Path)</span></div>
                        <button type="button" data-testid="file-select-@index" aria-label="View @file.Path" @onclick="() => ViewFileAsync(fileIndex)">View</button>
                    </li>
                }
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="card" data-testid="thread-index">
            <h2>Threads</h2>
            <div class="index-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter threads" data-testid="thread-summary">
                <button type="button" class="secondary" aria-pressed="@(IndexFilter is null ? "true" : "false")"
                        data-testid="index-filter-all" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(() => SetFilter(null))">All (<span data-testid="threads-all-count">@Threads.Count</span>)</button>
                <button type="button" class="secondary" aria-pressed="@(IndexFilter == ReviewThreadState.Open ? "true" : "false")"
                        data-testid="index-filter-open" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(() => SetFilter(ReviewThreadState.Open))">Open (<span data-testid="threads-open-count">@Threads.Count(t => t.State == ReviewThreadState.Open)</span>)</button>
                <button type="button" class="secondary" aria-pressed="@(IndexFilter == ReviewThreadState.Resolved ? "true" : "false")"
                        data-testid="index-filter-resolved" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(() => SetFilter(ReviewThreadState.Resolved))">Resolved (<span data-testid="threads-resolved-count">@Threads.Count(t => t.State == ReviewThreadState.Resolved)</span>)</button>
            </div>
            @{
                var indexRows = ThreadService.BuildIndex(Threads, IndexFilter);
            }
            @if (indexRows.Count == 0)
            {
                <p class="muted" data-testid="thread-index-empty">@IndexEmptyMessage()</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <ul class="item-list index-list" data-testid="thread-index-list">
                    @foreach (var row in indexRows)
                    {
                        var rowThread = row;
                        <li>
                            <button type="button" class="index-row" data-testid="index-row-@row.Id"
                                    aria-label="@IndexRowLabel(row)"
                                    @onclick="() => ViewThreadAsync(rowThread)">
                                <span class="path" data-testid="index-file-@row.Id">@row.FilePath</span>
                                <span data-testid="index-anchor-@row.Id">@AnchorLabel(row)</span>
                                <span class="badge @(row.State == ReviewThreadState.Resolved ? "resolved" : null)" data-testid="index-state-@row.Id">@row.State</span>
                                @if (ThreadHasUnread(row))
                                {
                                    <span class="badge unread" data-testid="index-unread-@row.Id">New</span>
                                }
                                <span class="muted" data-testid="index-count-@row.Id">@CommentCountLabel(row)</span>
                                <span class="muted" data-testid="index-author-@row.Id">@row.Comments.FirstOrDefault()?.Author</span>
                                <span class="muted" data-testid="index-activity-@row.Id">@FormatTime(row.LastActivity)</span>
                            </button>
                        </li>
                    }
                </ul>
            }
        </section>

        @if (SelectedPath is not null)
        {
            var fileThreads = Threads.Where(t => t.FilePath == SelectedPath).ToList();
            var focusedThread = fileThreads.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == FocusedThreadId && t.Side == ThreadSide.Head);
            var focusedBaselineThread = fileThreads.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == FocusedThreadId && t.Side == ThreadSide.Baseline);

            // In the diff the threads are drawn under their lines; only whole-file threads are listed below it
            var hasLineDiff = HasLineDiff;
            var listedThreads = hasLineDiff ? fileThreads.Where(t => t.StartLine is null).ToList() : fileThreads;
            var composerRange = hasLineDiff && !IsLocked ? ComposerRange() : null;
            var inlineComposer = composerRange is not null;
            ThreadSide? composerSide = inlineComposer ? NewSide : null;

            // Lines inside the range of a head thread are highlighted in the head view; the first line of a range
            // carries a count marker. Threads on the baseline side belong to the diff and the baseline view.
            var anchoredLines = new HashSet<int>();
            var startCounts = new Dictionary<int, int>();
            foreach (var thread in fileThreads.Where(t => t.StartLine is not null && t.Side == ThreadSide.Head))
            {
                for (var line = thread.StartLine!.Value; line <= thread.EndLine!.Value; line++)
                {
                    anchoredLines.Add(line);
                }

                startCounts[thread.StartLine!.Value] = startCounts.GetValueOrDefault(thread.StartLine!.Value) + 1;
            }

            // One thread: its header, comments, reply box and resolve control; used in the diff and in the list
            RenderFragment<ReviewThread> threadCard = item => @<li class="thread @(item.Id == FocusedThreadId ? "focused" : null)" data-testid="thread-@item.Id">
                @{
                    var threadId = item.Id;
                    var resolved = item.State == ReviewThreadState.Resolved;
                    var expanded = !resolved || ExpandedThreads.Contains(threadId);
                }
                <div class="thread-head">
                    <span class="path" data-testid="thread-anchor-@threadId">@AnchorLabel(item)</span>
                    <span class="badge @(resolved ? "resolved" : null)" data-testid="thread-state-@threadId">@item.State</span>
                    @if (ThreadHasUnread(item))
                    {
                        <span class="badge unread" data-testid="thread-unread-@threadId">New</span>
                    }
                    @if (item.CarriedFromReviewId is { } carriedFrom)
                    {
                        <span class="muted" data-testid="thread-carried-@threadId">carried from <a href="@ReviewLinks.ForReview(ProjectId, carriedFrom)" data-testid="thread-carried-link-@threadId">@carriedFrom</a></span>
                    }
                    <span class="muted" data-testid="thread-count-@threadId">@CommentCountLabel(item)</span>
                    <a class="thread-link action outline small" href="@ReviewLinks.ForThread(ProjectId, ReviewId, threadId)"
                       aria-label="Link to thread @threadId" data-testid="thread-link-@threadId">Link</a>
                    <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="thread-copy-link-@threadId"
                            aria-label="Copy link to thread @threadId"
                            @onclick="() => CopyThreadLinkAsync(threadId)">Copy link</button>
                    <span class="muted" role="status" data-testid="thread-copy-status-@threadId">@CopyStatusFor(threadId)</span>
                    @if (resolved)
                    {
                        <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="thread-expand-@threadId"
                                aria-expanded="@(expanded ? "true" : "false")"
                                aria-label="@(expanded ? "Collapse" : "Expand") thread @threadId"
                                @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(() => ToggleThreadExpanded(threadId))">@(expanded ? "Collapse" : "Expand")</button>
                    }
                    @if (expanded)
                    {
                        <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="thread-toggle-@threadId"
                                disabled="@IsLocked" data-locked="@LockedMarker"
                                aria-label="@(resolved ? "Reopen" : "Resolve") thread @threadId"
                                @onclick="() => ToggleThreadAsync(item)">@(resolved ? "Reopen" : "Resolve")</button>
                    }
                </div>
                @if (Warning?.Key == ToggleWarningKey(threadId))
                {
                    <SignatureWarning Slots="Warning.Slots" OnConfirm="ConfirmWarningAsync" OnCancel="CancelWarning" />
                }
                @if (expanded)
                {
                    @for (var n = 1; n <= item.Comments.Count; n++)
                    {
                        var comment = item.Comments[n - 1];
                        <div class="comment" data-testid="comment-@threadId-@n">
                            <div class="comment-meta">
                                <strong data-testid="comment-author-@threadId-@n">@comment.Author</strong>
                                <time class="muted" datetime="@comment.Created.UtcDateTime.ToString("O")" data-testid="comment-time-@threadId-@n">@FormatTime(comment.Created)</time>
                            </div>
                            <p class="comment-text" data-testid="comment-text-@threadId-@n">@comment.Text</p>
                        </div>
                    }
                    @if (!IsLocked)
                    {
                        <div class="reply">
                            <textarea id="reply-text-@threadId" rows="2" maxlength="@ReviewLimits.MaxCommentLength"
                                      aria-label="Reply to thread @threadId" placeholder="Reply"
                                      data-testid="reply-text-@threadId" value="@ReplyTexts.GetValueOrDefault(threadId)"
                                      data-ctrl-enter-submits="reply-button-@threadId"
                                      @oninput="e => ReplyTexts[threadId] = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty"></textarea>
                            @if (ReplyErrors.TryGetValue(threadId, out var replyError))
                            {
                                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="reply-error-@threadId">@replyError</p>
                            }
                            @if (Warning?.Key == ReplyWarningKey(threadId))
                            {
                                <SignatureWarning Slots="Warning.Slots" OnConfirm="ConfirmWarningAsync" OnCancel="CancelWarning" />
                            }
                            <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="reply-button-@threadId"
                                    aria-label="Post reply to thread @threadId"
                                    @onclick="() => ReplyAsync(threadId)">Reply</button>
                            <span class="muted hint" data-testid="reply-submit-hint-@threadId">Ctrl+Enter to submit</span>
                        </div>
                    }
                }
            </li>;

            // The new-thread form; in the diff it is drawn under the selected line, otherwise in its own card
            RenderFragment newThreadForm = @<form data-testid="new-thread-form" novalidate @onsubmit="StartThreadAsync">
                @if (CurrentView == FileView.Baseline && SelectedKind == ChangeKind.Deleted)
                {
                    <p class="muted hint" data-testid="deleted-comment-note">This file was deleted. A comment here applies to the whole file; use the Diff view to comment on a line.</p>
                }
                else if (CurrentView == FileView.Head)
                {
                    <div class="line-fields">
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="thread-start-line">Start line (optional)</label>
                            <input id="thread-start-line" type="number" min="1"
                                   data-testid="thread-start-line-input" @bind="NewStartLine" @bind:event="oninput" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="field">
                            <label for="thread-end-line">End line (optional)</label>
                            <input id="thread-end-line" type="number" min="1"
                                   data-testid="thread-end-line-input" @bind="NewEndLine" @bind:event="oninput" />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
                else if (inlineComposer)
                {
                    <div class="field through-field">
                        <label for="thread-end-line">Through line (optional)</label>
                        <input id="thread-end-line" type="number" min="1"
                               data-testid="thread-end-line-input" @bind="NewEndLine" @bind:event="oninput" />
                    </div>
                }
                <p class="muted hint" data-testid="thread-target">@NewThreadTarget().</p>
                <div class="field">
                    <label for="thread-text">Comment</label>
                    <textarea id="thread-text" rows="3" maxlength="@ReviewLimits.MaxCommentLength"
                              data-ctrl-enter-submits="start-thread-button"
                              data-testid="thread-text-input" @bind="NewText" @bind:event="oninput"></textarea>
                </div>
                @if (NewThreadError is not null)
                {
                    <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="thread-error">@NewThreadError</p>
                }
                @if (Warning?.Key == NewThreadWarningKey)
                {
                    <SignatureWarning Slots="Warning.Slots" OnConfirm="ConfirmWarningAsync" OnCancel="CancelWarning" />
                }
                <div class="form-actions">
                    <button type="submit" data-testid="start-thread-button">Start thread</button>
                    <span class="muted hint" data-testid="thread-submit-hint">Ctrl+Enter to submit</span>
                    @if (inlineComposer)
                    {
                        <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="thread-cancel-button" @onclick="CancelComment">Cancel</button>
                        <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="thread-whole-file-button" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(CommentOnWholeFile)">Comment on the whole file instead</button>
                    }
                </div>
            </form>;

            <section class="card">
                <h2>File content</h2>
                <p class="path" data-testid="selected-file-path">@SelectedPath</p>

                @if (Review.IsFromRepository)
                {
                    <p class="muted" data-testid="selected-file-kind">@SelectedKind</p>
                }

                @if (CanCompare)
                {
                    <div class="index-filters" role="group" aria-label="Which version of the file to show" data-testid="file-version-toggle">
                        <button type="button" class="secondary" aria-pressed="@(ShowingDiff ? "true" : "false")"
                                data-testid="view-diff-button" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(ShowDiff)">Diff</button>
                        @if (HasHeadVersion)
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="secondary" aria-pressed="@(CurrentView == FileView.Head ? "true" : "false")"
                                    data-testid="view-head-button" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(ShowHead)">Head</button>
                        }
                        @if (HasBaselineVersion)
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="secondary" aria-pressed="@(BaselineView ? "true" : "false")"
                                    data-testid="view-baseline-button" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(ShowBaselineAsync)">Baseline</button>
                        }
                    </div>
                }

                @if (ShowingDiff)
                {
                    @if (Diff!.Status == FileDiffStatus.Binary)
                    {
                        <p class="notice" data-testid="file-binary-notice">This is a binary file; its content is not shown.</p>
                    }
                    else if (Diff.Status == FileDiffStatus.TooLarge)
                    {
                        <div class="notice" data-testid="diff-too-large">
                            <p>Too large to compare line by line.</p>
                            <div class="index-filters">
                                @if (HasHeadVersion)
                                {
                                    <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="diff-too-large-head" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(ShowHead)">Show the Head version</button>
                                }
                                @if (HasBaselineVersion)
                                {
                                    <button type="button" class="secondary" data-testid="diff-too-large-baseline" @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(ShowBaselineAsync)">Show the Baseline version</button>
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <DiffView Result="Diff.Result!"
                                  OnlyLineEndingsDiffer="Diff.OnlyLineEndingsDiffer"
                                  Threads="fileThreads.Where(t => t.StartLine is not null).ToList()"
                                  FocusedThreadId="FocusedThreadId"
                                  HighlightSide="HighlightSide"
                                  HighlightLine="HighlightLine"
                                  SelectedSide="composerSide"
                                  SelectedStart="composerRange?.Start"
                                  SelectedEnd="composerRange?.End"
                                  ThreadTemplate="threadCard"
                                  Composer="newThreadForm"
                                  OnComment="request => GuardedAsync(() => CommentOnDiffLine(request))"
                                  CommentsDisabled="IsLocked"
                                  CanReveal="GuardChildAsync" />
                    }
                }
                else if (BaselineView)
                {
                    <p class="notice" data-testid="baseline-note">@(SelectedKind == ChangeKind.Deleted ? "Deleted file; this is its content at the baseline." : "Baseline (read-only). Use the Diff view to comment on these lines.")</p>
                    @if (BaselineLines is null)
                    {
                        <p class="notice" data-testid="file-binary-notice">This is a binary file; its content is not shown.</p>
                    }
                    else if (BaselineLines.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="notice" data-testid="file-empty-notice">This file is empty.</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="code" data-testid="baseline-content">
                            @for (var number = 1; number <= BaselineLines.Count; number++)
                            {
                                <div class="code-line @(IsFocusedLine(focusedBaselineThread, number) || (HighlightLine == number && HighlightSide == ThreadSide.Baseline) ? "focused" : null)" data-testid="baseline-line-@number">
                                    <span class="gutter">
                                        <span class="line-no" data-testid="baseline-line-no-@number">@number</span>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="line-text" data-testid="baseline-line-text-@number">@BaselineLines[number - 1]</span>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                }
                else if (SelectedLines is null)
                {
                    <p class="notice" data-testid="file-binary-notice">This is a binary file; its content is not shown.</p>
                }
                else if (SelectedLines.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="notice" data-testid="file-empty-notice">This file is empty, so it has no lines to comment on.</p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="code" data-testid="file-content">
                        @for (var number = 1; number <= SelectedLines.Count; number++)
                        {
                            var lineNumber = number;
                            <div class="code-line @(anchoredLines.Contains(number) ? "anchored" : null) @(IsFocusedLine(focusedThread, number) || (HighlightLine == number && HighlightSide == ThreadSide.Head) ? "focused" : null)" data-testid="code-line-@number">
                                <span class="gutter">
                                    <button type="button" class="line-comment" data-testid="line-comment-@number"
                                            disabled="@IsLocked" data-locked="@LockedMarker"
                                            aria-label="Comment on line @number" title="Comment on line @number"
                                            @onclick="() => GuardedAsync(() => CommentOnLine(lineNumber))">+</button>
                                    <span class="line-no" data-testid="line-no-@number">@number</span>
                                    <span class="line-marker">
                                        @if (startCounts.TryGetValue(number, out var markerCount))
                                        {
                                            <span class="thread-marker" data-testid="line-marker-@number" title="@markerCount thread(s) start here">@markerCount</span>
                                        }
                                    </span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="line-text" data-testid="line-text-@number">@SelectedLines[number - 1]</span>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </section>

            @if (!hasLineDiff || listedThreads.Count > 0)
            {
                <section class="card">
                    <h2>@(hasLineDiff ? "Comments on the whole file" : "Threads on this file")</h2>
                    @if (listedThreads.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="muted" data-testid="threads-empty">There are no threads on this file yet.</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <ul class="item-list threads" data-testid="threads-list">
                            @foreach (var listed in listedThreads)
                            {
                                @threadCard(listed)
                            }
                        </ul>
                    }
                </section>
            }

            @if (!inlineComposer && !IsLocked)
            {
                <section class="card">
                    <h2>@(CurrentView == FileView.Head ? "New thread" : "Comment on the whole file")</h2>
                    @if (BaselineView && SelectedKind != ChangeKind.Deleted)
                    {
                        <p class="muted" data-testid="baseline-comment-note">To comment on a line, switch to the Diff or Head view.</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        @newThreadForm
                    }
                </section>
            }
        }

        @if (reviewersCard is not null)
        {
            @reviewersCard
        }

        <details class="review-details" data-testid="review-details">
            <summary data-testid="review-details-summary">Details</summary>
            <dl class="details">
                <dt>Review id</dt>
                <dd data-testid="review-id">@Review.Id</dd>
                <dt>Fingerprint</dt>
                <dd class="hash" data-testid="review-fingerprint">@Review.ContentFingerprint</dd>
                @if (Review.IsFromRepository)
                {
                    <dt>Repository</dt>
                    <dd data-testid="review-repository">@Review.RepositoryName</dd>
                    @if (Review.ReviewSetId is not null)
                    {
                        <dt>Review set</dt>
                        <dd data-testid="review-set-id">@Review.ReviewSetId</dd>
                    }
                    <dt>Baseline</dt>
                    <dd class="hash" data-testid="review-baseline-sha">@(Review.BaselineSha ?? "none")</dd>
                    <dt>Head</dt>
                    <dd class="hash" data-testid="review-head-sha">@Review.HeadSha</dd>
                    <dt>Selection</dt>
                    <dd class="selection-text" data-testid="review-selection">@Review.Selection</dd>
                }
                @if (Approval is not null)
                {
                    <dt>Record digest</dt>
                    <dd class="hash" data-testid="record-digest" title="@Approval.Digest">@ShortDigest(Approval.Digest)</dd>
                }
                @for (var index = 0; index < Review.Files.Count; index++)
                {
                    <dt data-testid="file-hash-path-@index">@Review.Files[index].Path</dt>
                    <dd class="hash" data-testid="file-hash-@index">@Review.Files[index].Sha256</dd>
                }
            </dl>
        </details>
    }
</main>
</SessionGate>
